@0    = ~*sniffle*~ [FCHIL04]
@1    = ~Did you see my necklace?~
@2    = ~Excuse me, I don't have time to chat. I have to go and pick up my daughter from the Seatower Captain.~
@3    = ~My daughter! We had a look at the big chain in the Winch house and suddenly she was *gone*! I am so glad she was found so quickly. But now she is missing her necklace.~
@4    = ~*sigh* She must have lost her necklace while roaming around.~
@5    = ~Might it be this one, by any chance?~
@6    = ~(lie) Oh, such a pity. I think I saw your necklace—in the beak of a magpie, flying high over the towers!~
@7    = ~All right, I'll look for your necklace. Where could it be?~
@8    = ~And thankfully, none of this is my problem.~
@9    = ~A pity. Good day.~
@10   = ~Indeed. If you'll excuse us.~
@11   = ~Good day to you, too, <PRO_SIRMAAM>.~
@12   = ~Anywhere from here... to the apples!~
@13   = ~Darling, I think the good <PRO_MANWOMAN> needs a bit more specificity. Good <PRO_SIRMAAM>, I was told my daughter was found in one of the baskets in the East Tower, wherever that is, and I lost her in the Winch house. My assumption is that she must have lost her necklace somewhere between these two. But we already searched everywhere... I don't know what she means by "apples". I am sure she doesn't mean the kitchen. That cook makes sure no one goes in there! I would be very grateful if you could keep an eye out. She is very fond of that necklace.~
@14   = ~[Skie]I can *so* relate to that. I also used to have a necklace that I was *so* fond of.... Wait, where did that actually go?~
@15   = ~My necklace!~
@16   = ~Why yes, it is, indeed! Thank you so much for finding it—and returning it to us! What do you say, Melly?~
@17   = ~Thank you.~
@18   = ~Take this for compensation. Ah—we can finally go home! Come on, Melly. What an exciting day!~
@19   = ~[Imoen]Aww, did you see the look in her eyes? That was fun, <CHARNAME>!~
@20   = ~What? No! My necklace!~
@21   = ~[Imoen]Aww, did you see the hope die in her eyes? That was no fun, <CHARNAME>!~
@22   = ~[Jaheira]You have a cruel heart, <CHARNAME>.~
@23   = ~[Khalid]G-Gorion would not be proud, <CHARNAME>.~
@24   = ~Hmm, I'm not sure I like that look in your eyes, <PRO_SIRMAAM>, but the <PRO_MANWOMAN> has a point, Melly—we won't find the necklace again, at least not today. We're going home now. Come on, Melly. *sigh* What an exciting day.~
@25   = ~This girl was hiding in one of the baskets—right next to the stones for the trebuchets!~
@26   = ~It's all right. Your mom's already here.~
